8. @Scope - used to set the scope of a bean.

Idempotent - An operation is idempotent if performing it multiple times has the same effect as performing it once.

Together, they implement the CRUD operations in a RESTFUL API.
9.  @GetMapping    - Handles HTTP Get Request. Idempotent
                     Used to retrieve resources. Get the details of users.
                     It is faster than others.(Can Cache & give it to us if we hit same thing more time)
                     It cache like static one, like home page
10. @PostMapping   - Handles HTTP Post Request. Not Idempotent
                     Used to create new resources or submit data.
11. @PutMapping    - Handles HTTP Put Request. Idempotent
                     Used to update or replace an Existing resource
12. @DeleteMapping - Handles HTTP Delete Request. Idempotent
                     Used to delete the resource

